# SABOTAGE: T188 / issue #40 — the adapter-conformance positive control's fixture
# module is moved BACK below `defmodule Samen.AdapterConformanceCaseTest`, exactly where
# PR #34 left it. Nothing else changes: the same fixture, the same `adapter:`, the same
# assertions, the same 41 tests. Only the byte position of one `defmodule` moves.
#
# That position is the defect. `Samen.AdapterConformanceCaseTest` is `async: true`, and
# ExUnit takes an async module for execution as soon as the module's own `defmodule` has
# registered it with `ExUnit.Server` — i.e. WHILE the rest of that same file is still
# being compiled. With the fixture below the test module, the positive control races the
# compilation of its own fixture, and on the losing side `Code.ensure_loaded/1` answers
# `{:error, :nofile}` for a module that was never unloaded because it had not yet
# finished compiling.
#
# SEED-PINNED, deliberately. The defect is a compile-vs-run race, so it is not refutable
# at an arbitrary seed: the flip needs a seed that schedules that test early enough in
# the module's own shuffle. `--seed 5` does, and does so reliably — 14 of 14 runs of this
# file alone on unfixed `origin/main` flipped at that seed (and the full suite flips at
# `--seed 636821` and `--seed 12`, the seeds issue #40 was filed from). Hence the `--seed
# 5` in TEST_FILES: the harness's `mix test $test_files` word-splits, so the seed travels
# with the file. Without the pin this patch would flip only some of the time, which is
# the one thing a sabotage may not do.
#
# Flips the named positive control on the `Code.ensure_loaded/1` arm. Everything else in
# the file stays GREEN: the AdapterNotLoadedError red beside it, all three
# assert_refusal_table!/1 arms, both assert_masked_payload_only!/2 arms, the
# assert_masked_segments!/1 arms, load_fixtures!/1, assert_capture_no_leak!/2 and
# assert_redaction!/3 — so the failure is attributable to the fixture's placement alone.
#
# NOT TOUCHED, deliberately: `Samen.AdapterConformanceCase`'s `using/1` guard and its
# `Code.ensure_loaded?/1` check (the kit is correct; this was a test-ordering defect, not
# a kit defect), the `adapter:` module named (`Samen.Kms.FileBacked`, still real and still
# loaded), the precondition assertion on that adapter (it still passes — proving the flip
# is about the FIXTURE, not about the adapter), and the file's test count.
#
# The file still compiles under `--warnings-as-errors`: nothing is added or removed, only
# reordered.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/adapter_conformance_case_test.exs --seed 5
# MUST_FAIL: a REAL, loaded adapter module compiles cleanly (positive control)
diff --git a/samen_core/test/adapter_conformance_case_test.exs b/samen_core/test/adapter_conformance_case_test.exs
